# Ctrl-C and Escape over a streamed answer, and at an idle prompt: the exit
# hint on the hint row and its window (idle-cc, idle-cc-expired), a Ctrl-C
# mid-stream (cc-*) with the window across the turn's conclusion, the next
# turn answered normally, and Escape twice over a running turn (esc1, esc2).
# The answer streams words with no line break, so nothing of it is on the
# screen before the keystroke.
# The streamed turns arrive whole at once and hold their finish (`hangMs`),
# so every keystroke and snap mid-turn meets the same text on both binaries
# rather than whichever chunk a second's wait reached.
gateway interrupt-words.json
wait 2
key C-c
# The exit hint is snapped while it is up and once its 3 s are over, each
# by the screen rather than by a second count against them (FLAKE-HINT4).
until shown press ctrl+c again to exit
wait 0.3
snap idle-cc
# The frame itself holds the row it is for, or the run fails: the `until
# shown` before it was a look, and a wait came between (FLAKE-HINT4).
expect idle-cc press ctrl+c again to exit
wait 3.5
until gone press ctrl+c again to exit
snap idle-cc-expired
type stream please
key Enter
wait 2.5
snap mid
key C-c
until shown press ctrl+c again to exit
wait 0.3
snap cc-0.3
expect cc-0.3 press ctrl+c again to exit
wait 1.2
snap cc-1.5
expect cc-1.5 press ctrl+c again to exit
wait 2
until gone press ctrl+c again to exit
snap cc-3.5
type next
key Enter
wait 2
snap next
type stream again
key Enter
wait 2.5
snap mid2
key Escape
wait 0.3
snap esc1
wait 0.3
key Escape
wait 0.4
snap esc2
wait 1.5
snap esc2-later
snapfull end
gwlog
